tcd1304_array,diode_array,"Toshiba TCD1304DG/AP CCD linear image sensor datasheet (Toshiba Electronic Devices & Storage Corp., Rev.1.3, 2019-01-08), pixel geometry (Sec. 2, 8 um x 200 um, 3648 active pixels); Ocean Optics/Ocean Insight USB4000 Data Sheet (doc 211-00000-000-05-201210) for the as-operated full well (~100 ke-), read noise (~25 e- rms), 12-bit ADC, and default integration time (10 ms) this array is typically clocked at in that instrument","Physical linear-array counterpart to spectrometer_generic (same CCD, same detector_qe_table curve): render_diode_array bins the ideal detector-plane cube onto this array's REAL 8x200 um pixel geometry (3648 px) instead of spectrometer_generic's continuous resolution-convolved spectrum. full_well_e/read_noise_e/bit_depth/integration_time_s_default are typical USB4000-class OPERATING figures (the bare Toshiba chip datasheet does not itself specify a system full-well/read-noise/ADC in these terms -- those are instrument-level, from the USB4000 data sheet); adc_gain_e_per_dn=24.4 is DERIVED (full_well_e / (2**12-1), i.e. the gain that spans the full well over the 12-bit range) rather than a separately published number. stray_light_floor=5e-4 matches spectrometer_generic's own assumed grating-stray-light figure (same optical bench class). QE table is the identical digitized bare-chip curve as detector/tables/toshiba_tcd1304ap.mietab (copied per the per-registry tables convention -- see that table's own reference note for the ASSUMED 55% peak absolute-scale caveat; Toshiba only publishes RELATIVE response)",8.0,,,,,100000,25,,12,24.4,0.01,,,,,,,,,,,0.0005,tcd1304_qe.mietab,,,,,,,,200.0,3648
